**Findings**
1. **HOLD: idempotency is not a durable fence yet.** Idempotency, meaning a retry should return the prior result without doing work again, is specified as entity/content/client key in [L0 §6](/Users/jamesgiroux/Documents/dailyos-repo/.worktrees/codex/v1.4.5-w4-c-dos-474/.docs/plans/v1.4.5-workspace-memory/L0-packet-W4-C-DOS-474.md:193), but the proposed table only stores a final `receipt_json` and has no in-progress/reserved state. Existing ingestion guards only `(file_id, content_sha256, mode)` in [runs.rs](/Users/jamesgiroux/Documents/dailyos-repo/.worktrees/codex/v1.4.5-w4-c-dos-474/src-tauri/src/services/workspace_ingestion/runs.rs:7). Concurrent same-key calls can both write before either records a receipt.

2. **HOLD: service shape still lacks an entity path source.** The request carries `entity_type` and `entity_id` only in [L0 §4](/Users/jamesgiroux/Documents/dailyos-repo/.worktrees/codex/v1.4.5-w4-c-dos-474/.docs/plans/v1.4.5-workspace-memory/L0-packet-W4-C-DOS-474.md:123), but live path resolution requires an `entity_name` in [registry.rs](/Users/jamesgiroux/Documents/dailyos-repo/.worktrees/codex/v1.4.5-w4-c-dos-474/src-tauri/src/services/workspace_ingestion/registry.rs:416), and existing intake rejects missing names in [workspace_intake_impl.rs](/Users/jamesgiroux/Documents/dailyos-repo/.worktrees/codex/v1.4.5-w4-c-dos-474/src-tauri/src/services/workspace_ingestion/workspace_intake_impl.rs:178). L0 needs to name the entity lookup/slug source or choose an opaque path strategy.

3. **HOLD: fixed `workspace_ingestion` module shape is still unresolved.** The packet still allows a “replacement placement service file” / `mod.rs` change in [§7](/Users/jamesgiroux/Documents/dailyos-repo/.worktrees/codex/v1.4.5-w4-c-dos-474/.docs/plans/v1.4.5-workspace-memory/L0-packet-W4-C-DOS-474.md:227), but live `mod.rs` says downstream lanes never add submodules in [mod.rs](/Users/jamesgiroux/Documents/dailyos-repo/.worktrees/codex/v1.4.5-w4-c-dos-474/src-tauri/src/services/workspace_ingestion/mod.rs:4), enforced by [workspace_ingestion_mod_rs_shape.rs](/Users/jamesgiroux/Documents/dailyos-repo/.worktrees/codex/v1.4.5-w4-c-dos-474/src-tauri/tests/workspace_ingestion_mod_rs_shape.rs:3). Pick an existing file owner before L1.

4. **HOLD: transaction/cleanup is not chosen.** `IngestPipeline::run` writes lifecycle/run rows directly in [pipeline.rs](/Users/jamesgiroux/Documents/dailyos-repo/.worktrees/codex/v1.4.5-w4-c-dos-474/src-tauri/src/services/workspace_ingestion/pipeline.rs:150). An outer `ActionDb::with_transaction` can work because nested calls collapse in [core.rs](/Users/jamesgiroux/Documents/dailyos-repo/.worktrees/codex/v1.4.5-w4-c-dos-474/src-tauri/src/db/core.rs:99), but file writes cannot roll back. L0 leaves cleanup vs failed/quarantined lifecycle open in [§5](/Users/jamesgiroux/Documents/dailyos-repo/.worktrees/codex/v1.4.5-w4-c-dos-474/.docs/plans/v1.4.5-workspace-memory/L0-packet-W4-C-DOS-474.md:189).

5. **HOLD: migration slot v266 is not coordination-clean.** Live code ends at v259 in [migrations.rs](/Users/jamesgiroux/Documents/dailyos-repo/.worktrees/codex/v1.4.5-w4-c-dos-474/src-tauri/src/migrations.rs:1018), and v1.4.5 claims W4 v266-v267 in [v1.4.5-waves.md](/Users/jamesgiroux/Documents/dailyos-repo/.worktrees/codex/v1.4.5-w4-c-dos-474/.docs/plans/v1.4.5-waves.md:235). But v1.4.6 still reserves v260-v279 and specifically v265-v266 in [v1.4.6-waves.md](/Users/jamesgiroux/Documents/dailyos-repo/.worktrees/codex/v1.4.5-w4-c-dos-474/.docs/plans/v1.4.6-waves.md:327). Also `account-fact-claim-producer` edits `migrations.rs` and adds v260.

6. **HOLD: MCP route conflicts are real and under-specified.** The live handler registry currently registers only account status in [registration.rs](/Users/jamesgiroux/Documents/dailyos-repo/.worktrees/codex/v1.4.5-w4-c-dos-474/src-tauri/src/services/mcp_v2/handlers/registration.rs:39), while gateway dispatch requires a registered handler in [gateway.rs](/Users/jamesgiroux/Documents/dailyos-repo/.worktrees/codex/v1.4.5-w4-c-dos-474/src-tauri/src/services/mcp_v2/gateway.rs:300). PR #355 touches gateway/contracts/handler registration files; #366 also touches context, gateway, handler, migrations, and account/Glean code. The packet’s coordination note is directionally right but needs exact file ownership and sequencing.

7. **AMEND: dual rate limit is not supported by current gateway shape.** L0 requires 10/minute and 200/hour in [§3](/Users/jamesgiroux/Documents/dailyos-repo/.worktrees/codex/v1.4.5-w4-c-dos-474/.docs/plans/v1.4.5-workspace-memory/L0-packet-W4-C-DOS-474.md:69), but `mcp_tool_grant` stores one `rate_limit_max/window` and `reserve_rate_limit` enforces one window in [gateway.rs](/Users/jamesgiroux/Documents/dailyos-repo/.worktrees/codex/v1.4.5-w4-c-dos-474/src-tauri/src/services/mcp_v2/gateway.rs:604). Needs a schema/logic amendment.

**Verdict: HOLD.** No files edited.